('5WiFcYk','Weighted Lunge with Swing','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'weighted',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a weight in each hand.','Step forward with your right foot, lowering your body into a lunge position.','Set the shoulders and let the weight move back between the legs as the hips hinge.','Hinge back, then drive the hips forward to send the weight up; let the arms guide it.','Let the hips, not the shoulders, provide the power.','Let the weight fall naturally and hinge again for the next swing.'],0),
('61GrD55','Cable Lying Close-Grip Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Connect a straight bar to a low pulley cable machine.','Lie face up on a flat bench with your feet planted.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('62Nw60O','Barbell Rear Lunge','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell across your upper back.','Step backward with your right foot, landing on the ball of your foot.','Set your stance wide enough to balance before bending either knee.','Step into the movement and bend both knees, keeping your front foot planted.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
('641mIfk','Barbell Incline Reverse-Grip Press','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Recline on the bench and Hold the barbell with a reverse grip, hands just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the palms in the chosen grip without bending the wrists back.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('67n3r98','Machine Shoulder Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','pectorals'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles with palms facing down and position your hands at shoulder level.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('6bOA1Oi','Weighted Side Bend (On Stability Ball)','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','erector spinae'],'weighted',array['Take a seat on a stability ball with your feet about shoulder width and flat on the ground.','Take a weight in one hand and place your other hand on your hip.','Stand or sit tall with the pelvis facing forward.','Bend sideways through the waist without twisting or letting the hips shift.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('6cKQC5E','Dumbbell Single-Arm Upright Row','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','biceps'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in one hand with palms facing down.','Let the dumbbell hang at arm''s length ahead of your thighs, with your palm facing your body.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('6CKUx7o','Ez-Bar Lying Close-Grip Triceps Extension Behind Head','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'EZ bar',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your head at the end of the bench.','Take hold of the ez barbell with a close grip, palms facing up, and extend your arms straight up over your chest.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('6e2DcYX','Dumbbell Incline Shoulder Raise','chest','serratus anterior',array['deltoids','trapezius'],'dumbbell',array['Angle an incline bench to a 45-degree angle and sit on it with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing down.','Set the dumbbells on your thighs and lean back onto the bench.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the weights away from your torso to about shoulder height, keeping the elbows softly bent.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('6em2Dxj','Dumbbell Alternate Seated Hammer Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your torso and arms extended down.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and your elbows close to your torso.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl with palms facing each other and elbows near your sides; avoid rocking back.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('6FMU51h','Semi Squat Jump','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Before moving, bend your knees and lower your body into a squat position.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('6HiHHe0','Barbell Standing Rocking Leg Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','quadriceps'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell across your upper back.','Before moving, raise your heels off the ground as high as possible, balancing on the balls of your feet.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('6HmFgmx','Standing Calf Raise (On a Staircase)','lower legs','calves',array['ankles','feet'],'bodyweight',array['Step onto the edge of a step or a sturdy platform with your heels hanging off and your toes on the step.','Use a railing or wall for balance if needed.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('6kSxYnw','Barbell Wrist Curl','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','brachialis'],'barbell',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; your knees bent.','Take a barbell with palms facing up, and your hands about shoulder width.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('6MaEjVA','Smith Standing Leg Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'smith machine',array['Set the smith machine bar to a height that allows you to stand with your feet planted and your shoulders under the bar.','Set yourself under the bar with your feet about shoulder width and your toes pointing forward.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('6MfS53i','Dumbbell Lying Single Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a bench with a dumbbell in one hand and your arm straight above your chest.','Lower the dumbbell in a controlled manner toward your forehead, keeping your upper arm stationary.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('6pTkI99','Dumbbell Single-Arm Snatch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps','core'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in one hand with palms facing down.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady and chest up.','Brace before the pull and keep the load close to the body.','Drive through the legs and hips, then guide the weight to its receiving position.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Stand tall to finish, then lower the weight under control before the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('6sMAmNv','Dumbbell Reverse Spider Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body and arms straight.','With your upper arms stationary, exhale and curl the weights while contracting your biceps.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl the weight with your palms facing down, keeping the elbows close and torso still.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('6sYyrRX','Bent Knee Lying Twist','upper legs','glutes',array['obliques','hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Reach your arms out to the sides, perpendicular to your body.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the turn smooth instead of throwing the arms across the body.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('6t00BsF','Cable Single-Arm Incline Press on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'cable',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with your feet planted and your back resting against an incline bench.','Take a cable handle in one hand and position your arm at a 90-degree angle with your elbow bent.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('6TG6x2w','Ez-Bar Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'EZ bar',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold the ez barbell with palms facing up.','Hold your elbows near your torso and your upper arms stationary throughout the movement.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('6YUfHPL','Quads (Bodyweight Squat)','upper legs','quadriceps',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Before moving, lower your body by bending your knees and pushing your hips back as if sitting on a chair.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
