('7aolH9D','Medicine Ball Chest Push Multiple Response','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'medicine ball',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a medicine ball at chest level.','Reach your arms forward, pushing the medicine ball away from your chest.','Set a firm stance and leave enough clear space for the ball to travel.','Drive the ball away forcefully, using the arms and trunk together; catch or retrieve it before resetting.','Follow through with the whole body while keeping control of the landing or catch.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('7aVz15j','Triceps Dips Floor','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on the edge of a chair or bench with your hands next to your hips, fingers pointing forward.','Move your butt off the front of the chair with your legs extended in front of you.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
