('8eqjhOl','Dumbbell Palms in Incline Bench Press','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Take a seat on the bench with your back against the backrest and feet planted.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('8fgqP5a','Dumbbell Standing Single-Arm Concentration Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in one hand, palm facing up.','Set your free hand on your thigh for support.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('8K0w2yA','Assisted Hanging Knee Raise with Throw Down','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','erector spinae'],'assisted',array['Suspend yourself from a pull-up bar with your arms straight and your palms turned away from you.','Brace your trunk and lift your knees toward your chest, keeping your legs together.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Slow the legs before they pull the lower back out of position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('8K7m2SS','Medicine Ball Close-Grip Push Up','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'medicine ball',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands on the medicine ball, about shoulder width.','Lower your body toward the ground by bending your elbows, keeping them close to your sides.','Brace the abdomen and glutes so the shoulders, hips and ankles move together.','Bend your elbows to lower your chest while keeping your body in one line.','Keep the head in line with the spine as the elbows bend.','Press back to straight arms, keeping the body line intact.'],0),
('8oYqOt9','Cable Seated Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Take a seat on a cable machine with your feet planted and your back straight.','Hold the cable attachment with palms facing up, and your arms straight.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('8ozhUIZ','Barbell Standing Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and place a barbell across your upper back.','Before moving, raise your heels off the ground as high as possible, using only your toes.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('8urJS9b','Weighted Hyperextension (On Stability Ball)','back','erector spinae',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'weighted',array['Set yourself face down on a stability ball with your hips resting on the ball and your feet against a wall for stability.','Set your hands behind your head or cross them over your chest.','Secure the hips and feet on the support before lifting.','Raise your torso or legs until they line up with your body, without arching sharply at the lower back.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Return along the same path at a controlled pace.'],0),
('8xUv4J7','Cable Seated Crunch','waist','abdominals',array['obliques'],'cable',array['Take a seat on a cable machine with your feet planted and your knees bent.','Take hold of the cable handle with both hands and position it behind your head.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('903mzG8','Smith Shoulder Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','upper back'],'smith machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the bar with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('945zpRg','Barbell Wide Reverse-Grip Bench Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your back pressed against the bench.','Hold the barbell with a wide reverse grip, just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the palms in the chosen grip without bending the wrists back.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('99rWm7w','Hamstring Stretch','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Move forward with your right foot and shift your weight onto your right leg.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('9Ap7miY','Decline Crunch','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto a decline bench with your feet secured and your knees bent at a 90-degree angle.','Set your hands behind your head or across your chest.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('9c6T1YX','Bridge - Mountain Climber (Cross Body)','waist','abdominals',array['glutes','quadriceps','hamstrings','deltoids','triceps'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body in a straight line.','Brace your trunk and lift your right foot off the ground, bringing your right knee toward your left elbow.','Brace the trunk lightly before moving a limb.','Move the working arm or leg while keeping the trunk steady and the breathing even.','Keep the pelvis from rocking as the arm or leg moves.','Reset your posture before changing sides or beginning the next rep.'],0),
('9E25EOx','Split Squats','upper legs','quadriceps',array['glutes','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Step forward with one foot and place it about two feet in front of the other foot.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('9gbyYKk','Band Seated Hip Internal Rotation','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps'],'resistance band',array['Take a seat on a chair or bench with your back straight and feet planted.','Set a resistance band around your thighs, just above your knees.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('9GXrTE6','Smith Single-Leg Floor Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'smith machine',array['Set yourself on the floor under the smith machine bar, turned away from the machine.','Set the balls of your feet on a raised surface, such as a weight plate or block.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Keep the pelvis level as the supporting leg does the work.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('9IxJdtC','Lying Leg-Hip Raise','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your legs extended and your arms by your sides.','Set your hands under your glutes for support.','Plant the feet and keep the ribs from flaring as the hips prepare to rise.','Press through the feet and lift your hips until your torso and thighs line up.','Stop when the hips line up with the torso; do not arch higher through the lower back.','Lower the hips steadily and keep the feet planted for the next lift.'],0),
('9JprnPh','Band Single Leg Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['ankles','feet'],'resistance band',array['Stand and set your feet about hip width and place the band around the ball of your left foot.','Use a stable object for balance if needed.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('9KU9TYF','Machine Horizontal Single-Leg Press','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'leverage machine',array['Set the seat of the machine so that your knees are at a 90-degree angle when your feet are on the footplate.','Take a seat on the machine with your back against the backrest and your feet about shoulder width on the footplate.','Set your feet firmly on the plate and keep the hips against the seat.','Bend the knees to bring the platform toward you, then press it away through the feet.','Keep the pelvis level as the supporting leg does the work.','Return along the same path at a controlled pace; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('9n2149Z','Sled Lying Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'sled machine',array['Set the sled machine to a comfortable weight.','Settle onto your back on the sled machine with your feet on the footplate.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('9pa4H5m','Band Horizontal Pallof Press','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','glutes'],'resistance band',array['Connect the band to a sturdy anchor point at waist height.','Stand perpendicular to the anchor point with your feet about shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('9pQSkH8','Dumbbell Reverse-Grip Incline Bench Two-Arm Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Take a seat on the bench with your chest against the backrest and your feet planted.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep the palms in the chosen grip without bending the wrists back.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('9RT8oQW','Bench Dip on Floor','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on the edge of a bench or chair with your hands gripping the edge, fingers pointing forward.','Move your butt off the bench, supporting your weight with your hands.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('9sgNE2O','Barbell Decline Pullover','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Get onto a decline bench with your head lower than your hips and your feet secured.','Take hold of the barbell with a pronated grip (palms turned away from you) and your hands just beyond shoulder width.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ribs down as the arms travel overhead.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('9Tkqa9O','Kettlebell Windmill','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','deltoids'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a kettlebell in your right hand overhead.','Before moving, rotate your left foot outwards about 45 degrees and keep your right foot pointing forward.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the turn smooth instead of throwing the arms across the body.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('9WTm7dq','Chest Dip','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Set yourself on parallel bars with your arms straight and your body straight.','Before moving, lower your body by bending your elbows until your shoulders are below your elbows.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('9XjtHvS','Dumbbell Pullover','chest','pectorals',array['latissimus dorsi','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your head at one end and your feet on the floor.','Take a dumbbell with both hands and extend your arms straight above your chest.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ribs down as the arms travel overhead.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('9ZGZuOD','Incline Twisting Sit-Up','waist','abdominals',array['obliques'],'bodyweight',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Get onto the bench with your feet secured under the foot pads.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('A2upspL','Single-Leg Donkey Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes pointing forward.','Set your hands on a stable surface for support, such as a wall or a bar.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Keep the pelvis level as the supporting leg does the work.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('a4F9Oyc','Kettlebell Double Alternating Hang Clean','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms','deltoids'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a kettlebell in each hand with palms facing down.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady and chest up.','Brace before the pull and keep the load close to the body.','Drive through the legs and hips, then guide the weight to its receiving position.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Stand tall to finish, then lower the weight under control before the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('A6wtbuL','Dumbbell Standing Overhead Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','upper back'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand at shoulder level with your palms facing forward.','Press the dumbbells upward until your arms are straight overhead.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('a8VDgLw','Stationary Bike Walk','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'leverage machine',array['Set the seat height and position on the stationary bike to ensure proper alignment.','Set your feet on the pedals and secure them with the straps if available.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Move at a repeatable pace, keeping the motion smooth and your breathing steady.','Keep the pattern repeatable as speed increases.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],4),
('A9qxk2F','Archer Push Up','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids','core'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a push-up position with your hands just beyond shoulder width.','Reach one arm straight out to the side, parallel to the ground.','Brace the abdomen and glutes so the shoulders, hips and ankles move together.','Shift toward one hand and bend that elbow while the other arm straightens to the side.','Keep the head in line with the spine as the elbows bend.','Press back to straight arms, keeping the body line intact.'],0),
('aaxA3cm','Smith Reverse-Grip Bent Over Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'smith machine',array['Prepare the smith machine with the bar at hip height.','Face the bar from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep the palms in the chosen grip without bending the wrists back.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('aaXr7ld','Machine T Bar Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'leverage machine',array['Set the seat height and footplate position to ensure proper alignment.','Take a seat on the machine with your chest against the pad and your feet flat on the footplate.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('aDoFKrE','Medicine Ball Chest Pass','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'medicine ball',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding the medicine ball at chest level.','Reach your arms forward, pushing the medicine ball away from your chest with force.','Set a firm stance and leave enough clear space for the ball to travel.','Drive the ball away forcefully, using the arms and trunk together; catch or retrieve it before resetting.','Follow through with the whole body while keeping control of the landing or catch.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('ae9UoXQ','Dumbbell Incline Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Angle an incline bench to a 45-degree angle and sit on it with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing forward.','Set your upper arms on the incline bench and let your elbows hang down, straighten your arms.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('aee2Fcj','Barbell Biceps Curl (With Arm Blaster)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'barbell',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell with palms facing up.','Set your upper arms against the arm blaster, keeping your elbows close to your torso.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('Af0EW2I','Muscle-Up (On Vertical Bar)','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','triceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Begin by hanging from a vertical bar with your palms turned away from you and your arms straight.','Brace your trunk and pull your body up toward the bar, leading with your chest.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('aHDy5O5','Band Y-Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','rhomboids'],'resistance band',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold the band ahead of your thighs with your palms facing inwards.','Maintain straight arms and lift them up and out to the sides, forming a ''Y'' shape with your body.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Raise the arms diagonally into a Y shape while keeping the shoulders away from your ears.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('ainizkb','Dumbbell Upright Row','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','biceps'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with palms facing down.','Let the dumbbells hang ahead of your thighs, with your arms straight.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('Al3tP0D','Medicine Ball Supine Chest Throw','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'medicine ball',array['Settle onto your back on a bench with your knees bent and feet planted.','Take hold of the medicine ball with both hands, extending your arms straight up above your chest.','Brace and settle into a stable starting position.','Move through the intended path under control, keeping the joints aligned with the resistance.','Keep the movement controlled throughout the range.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('Am02iPd','Dumbbell Single-Arm Fly on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with a dumbbell in one hand and your feet planted.','Step your feet forward and roll your body down until your upper back is resting on the exercise ball.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('ANbbry2','Lower Back Curl','back','erector spinae',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your stomach with your legs extended and your arms by your sides.','Engage your glutes and hamstrings, and With control lift your upper body off the ground, curling your back upwards.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('AQ0mC4Y','Dumbbell Full Can Lateral Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','rotator cuff'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing your body.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and Brace your trunk.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Raise the arms out to the sides to about shoulder height without leaning or shrugging.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('AQIhRjM','Lying Elbow to Knee','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','erector spinae'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands behind your head with your elbows pointing outwards.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('aqvSOQE','Cable Crossover Reverse Fly','shoulders','deltoids',array['rhomboids','trapezius'],'cable',array['Connect a D-handle to each low pulley cable and stand in the middle of the cable crossover machine.','Hold the handles with a pronated grip (palms facing down) and take a step forward, positioning your feet about shoulder width.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','Bring the handles across the front of your chest in a broad arc, keeping a slight elbow bend.','Keep the elbow angle nearly unchanged through the arc.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load.'],0),
