('awG04cF','Finger Curls','lower arms','forearms',array['wrist flexors','grip muscles'],'barbell',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; hold a barbell with palms facing up.','Set your forearms on your thighs, letting your wrists hang off the edge.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Let the bar roll toward your fingertips, then close your fingers firmly around it.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('AX1kB0o','Twist Hip Lift','upper legs','glutes',array['obliques','hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands by your sides for support.','Plant the feet and keep the ribs from flaring as the hips prepare to rise.','Press through the feet and lift your hips until your torso and thighs line up.','Stop when the hips line up with the torso; do not arch higher through the lower back.','Lower the hips steadily and keep the feet planted for the next lift.'],0),
('aXcUyKb','Kettlebell Single-Arm Snatch','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','forearms','core'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a kettlebell in one hand between your legs.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge at the hips, lowering the kettlebell toward the ground.','Brace before the pull and keep the load close to the body.','Drive through the legs and hips, then guide the weight to its receiving position.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Stand tall to finish, then lower the weight under control before the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('AxFoqAD','Hack Single-Leg Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'sled machine',array['Set the sled machine to an appropriate weight.','Step onto the sled machine with one foot, keeping the other foot off the ground.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Keep the pelvis level as the supporting leg does the work.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('aXtJhlg','Dumbbell Step-Up','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'dumbbell',array['Take your place in front of a bench or step with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body.','Set your right foot on the bench or step, ensuring your entire foot is in contact with the surface.','Put the lead foot fully on the platform before shifting your weight onto it.','Step onto the platform and drive through the lead foot to stand tall on it.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
('ayAHcEm','Smith Incline Shoulder Raises','chest','serratus anterior',array['deltoids','trapezius'],'smith machine',array['Set the smith machine to an incline position.','Face the machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the weights away from your torso to about shoulder height, keeping the elbows softly bent.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('B1EVP9F','Incline Push-Up','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Set your hands on an elevated surface, such as a bench or step, just beyond shoulder width.','Reach your legs behind you, resting on the balls of your feet, creating a straight line from your head to your heels.','Brace the abdomen and glutes so the shoulders, hips and ankles move together.','Bend your elbows to lower your chest while keeping your body in one line.','Keep the head in line with the spine as the elbows bend.','Press back to straight arms, keeping the body line intact.'],0),
('b2Uoz54','Barbell Front Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['biceps','triceps'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell ahead of your thighs with palms facing down.','Maintain straight arms and lift the barbell forward and upward until it reaches shoulder level.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the arms forward to about shoulder height, keeping the ribs down and torso still.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('B3Rxp6L','Dumbbell Incline Bench Press','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Take a seat on the bench with your back against the pad and feet planted.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],43),
('b4b6afT','Weighted Seated Biceps Curl (On Stability Ball)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'medicine ball',array['Take a seat on a stability ball with your feet planted and your back straight.','Take a medicine ball with palms facing up, and let your arms hang down by your sides.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('B5xca8s','Hands Clasped Circular Toe Touch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your hands clasped together ahead of your chest.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady.','Soften the knees and let the hips start the fold.','Fold forward from the hips and let your hands travel toward your feet without forcing the reach.','Keep the movement controlled throughout the range.','Hold briefly at a comfortable depth, then rise by extending the hips.'],0),
('b63ZzGe','Potty Squat with Support','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes pointing slightly outward.','Use a stable support, such as a chair or wall, for balance.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('B6dAO1t','Smith Seated Wrist Curl','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','brachialis'],'smith machine',array['Take a seat on a bench in front of a Smith machine with your feet planted.','Hold the barbell with palms facing up, hands about shoulder width.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('b6hQYMb','Machine Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Set your upper arms on the pad and grip the handles with palms facing up.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('b9kqlBy','Kettlebell Alternating Renegade Row','back','upper back',array['core','deltoids'],'kettlebell',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands gripping the kettlebells and your feet about hip width.','Brace your trunk and keep your body in a straight line from head to heels.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('BaE7O6U','Hanging Oblique Knee Raise','waist','abdominals',array['obliques'],'bodyweight',array['Suspend yourself from a pull-up bar with your arms straight and your palms turned away from you.','Brace your trunk and lift your knees toward your chest, twisting your torso to the side as you do so.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Slow the legs before they pull the lower back out of position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('BbfB8Gb','Standing Toe Touch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your arms by your sides.','Bend forward at the waist, with your spine steady and your knees soft.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Fold forward from the hips and let your hands travel toward your feet without forcing the reach.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold briefly at a comfortable depth, then rise by extending the hips.'],0),
('bBi35y3','Dumbbell Standing Alternate Overhead Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','core'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand at shoulder level with your palms facing forward.','Before moving, press one dumbbell overhead, fully extending your arm.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('bbLR7fB','Band Lying Straight-Leg Raise','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'resistance band',array['Settle onto your back with your legs straight and your feet together.','Set the band around the arches of your feet and hold the ends of the band with your hands.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('BCGQ6J5','Cable Close-Grip Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Connect a straight bar to a low pulley cable machine.','Face the machine with your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('BCs0G2F','Barbell Seated Alternate Leg Raise','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','quadriceps'],'barbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with your back straight and hold a barbell across your thighs.','Set your hands on the sides of the bench for support.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('BCUR88E','Dumbbell Standing Single-Arm Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in one hand.','Before moving, raise the dumbbell overhead, fully extending your arm.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('bd5b860','Wrist Rollerer','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','triceps'],'weighted',array['Connect a weight to one end of a rope or bar.','Take hold of the other end of the rope or bar with both hands, palms facing down.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
