('bmwlYvD','Gorilla Chin','waist','abdominals',array['forearms','biceps'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Hold a pull-up bar with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('Bn6TXyO','Sit-Up','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands behind your head with your elbows pointing outwards.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('bndCa3Q','Barbell Pin Presses','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'barbell',array['Prepare a barbell on a power rack at chest height.','Face the barbell and position yourself underneath it, from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
