('BWnJR72','Lying (Side) Quads Stretch','upper legs','quadriceps',array['hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your side with your legs straight.','Before moving, bend your top leg and grab your ankle or foot with your hand.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('BwSNDGt','Dumbbell Single-Arm Reverse Wrist Curl','lower arms','forearms',array['wrist extensors'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench or chair with your feet planted.','Take a dumbbell in one hand with palms facing down, palm facing down.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('bWxq4op','Dumbbell Single-Arm Reverse Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a preacher bench with your chest against the pad and your arm extended over the edge of the bench, holding a dumbbell with palms facing up.','Lower the dumbbell With control until your arm is straight.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('ByX0WxV','Dumbbell Incline Hammer Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your torso and arms straight.','Keep your back against the bench and your feet planted.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl with palms facing each other and elbows near your sides; avoid rocking back.','Keep the palms facing each other and the wrists straight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('bZGHsAZ','Inverted Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Prepare a bar at waist height or use a suspension trainer.','Face the bar or suspension trainer, from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('bZq4bwK','Weighted Triceps Dips','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'weighted',array['Take a seat on the edge of a bench or chair with your hands gripping the edge next to your hips.','Move your butt off the front of the bench with your legs extended in front of you.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('C0eCeEt','Twisted Leg Raise','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your legs extended and your arms by your sides.','Set your hands under your glutes for support.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Slow the legs before they pull the lower back out of position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('C0MA9bC','Dumbbell Single-Arm Bent-Over Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in one hand with your palm facing your body.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady and your core engaged.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],20),
('c16nYGA','Band Single-Arm Twisting Chest Press','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'resistance band',array['Connect the band to a sturdy anchor point at chest height.','Stand and set your side facing the anchor point and grab the band with one hand.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weights up while turning the palms inward; reverse the turn as you lower.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('C31LMnP','Single-Leg Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Reach one leg forward, keeping it off the ground.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Keep the pelvis level as the supporting leg does the work.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('c3Pfhti','Roller Side Lat Stretch','back','latissimus dorsi',array['deltoids','triceps'],'roller',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold the roller with both hands ahead of your body.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('c3QQLPi','Cable Rear Drive','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids','back'],'cable',array['Connect a handle to a low pulley cable machine and stand turned away from the machine.','Hold the handle with palms facing down and extend your arms straight out in front of you.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('C5jncD2','Standing Single Leg Curl','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about hip width and your hands on your hips.','Transfer your weight onto your left leg and lift your right foot off the ground, bending your knee.','Line the knees up with the machine or bench edge before starting the curl.','Bend your knees to draw the pad toward you without lifting your hips from the support.','Keep the hips still while the knees bend.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('c8f5cSY','Side-Lying Hip Adduction','upper legs','adductors',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your side with your legs straight and stacked on top of each other.','Set your bottom arm under your head for support.','Square the pelvis before moving the working leg.','Draw the working leg inward against resistance without leaning sideways.','Move only as far as the pelvis can remain steady.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('c8oybX6','Cable Rope Elevated Seated Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'cable',array['Take a seat on the elevated seat facing the cable machine.','Take a rope end in each hand with the palms facing each other.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('C9LuR4A','Machine Donkey Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'leverage machine',array['Set the leverage machine to the appropriate height for your body.','Set yourself facing the machine, with your toes on the foot platform and your heels hanging off the edge.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('c9MnDRp','Dumbbell Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','rhomboids'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and Brace your trunk.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the weights away from your torso to about shoulder height, keeping the elbows softly bent.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('Ca76jUE','Kettlebell Alternating Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, knees soft, and hold a kettlebell in each hand with your palms facing your body.','Bend forward at the hips, with your spine steady and your core engaged.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('cA9FuWG','Barbell Bent Arm Pullover','back','latissimus dorsi',array['triceps','pectorals'],'barbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your head at one end and your feet on the floor.','Take a barbell with a shoulder-width grip and extend your arms straight above your chest.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ribs down as the arms travel overhead.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('cALkHHX','Dumbbell Iron Cross','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','pectorals'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand at your sides.','Before moving, raise your arms out to the sides until they are parallel to the ground, forming a T shape with your body.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Open the arms out to the sides to form a T, then bring them back under control.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('cALKspW','Cable Upright Row','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','biceps'],'cable',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, knees soft, and hold the cable attachment with palms facing down.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and your core engaged throughout the exercise.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('cAvTaSg','Dumbbell Kickbacks on Exercise Ball','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids','back'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with your feet planted and your back straight.','Take a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing inwards and your arms bent at a 90-degree angle.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Hold the upper arm beside your torso and straighten the elbow behind you.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('CB8WET1','Incline Push Up Depth Jump','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids','core'],'bodyweight',array['Choose an elevated surface, such as a bench or step, and place your hands about shoulder width on the edge.','Move your feet back, keeping your body in a straight line from head to heels.','Brace the abdomen and glutes so the shoulders, hips and ankles move together.','Bend your elbows to lower your chest while keeping your body in one line.','Keep the head in line with the spine as the elbows bend.','Press back to straight arms, keeping the body line intact.'],0),
('CbFSYC1','Rear Pull-Up','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Take hold of the pull-up bar with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Suspend yourself from the bar with your arms straight and your body straight.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull up with control, keeping the head neutral and the elbows moving down beside the torso.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('cbuFJrn','Machine Gripless Shrug','back','trapezius',array['deltoids','forearms'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles or bars with palms facing down, keeping your arms straight.','Let the arms hang long and keep the head neutral.','Lift your shoulders toward your ears without bending the elbows or rolling the shoulders.','Lift and lower vertically without circling the shoulders.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('CcWEoWV','Short Stride Run','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Choose an open space or a treadmill to perform the exercise.','Stand tall and set your feet about hip width.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Move at a repeatable pace, keeping the motion smooth and your breathing steady.','Keep the pattern repeatable as speed increases.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],0),
('CfKsRbG','Dumbbell Alternate Biceps Curl (With Arm Blaster)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing forward.','Set the arm blaster on your upper arms, ensuring a secure fit.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('CFN9P8G','Ez-Bar French Press on Exercise Ball','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'EZ bar',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball and hold an EZ barbell with palms facing down.','Reach your arms straight up, keeping your elbows close to your head.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Bend the elbows to lower the bar behind your head while the upper arms stay mostly still.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Straighten the elbows to bring the bar overhead, then begin the next controlled rep.'],0),
('CggQhII','Machine Military Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','pectorals'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles with palms facing down and position your hands just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('chfnQnM','Back Pec Stretch','back','latissimus dorsi',array['deltoids','pectorals'],'bodyweight',array['Stand tall and set your feet about shoulder width.','Reach your arms straight out in front of you, parallel to the ground.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('CHpahtl','Machine Seated Hip Abduction','upper legs','abductors',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'leverage machine',array['Set the seat height so that your knees are at a 90-degree angle.','Take a seat on the machine with your back against the backrest and your feet on the footrests.','Square the pelvis before moving the working leg.','Open the knees or legs against resistance without shifting your torso.','Move only as far as the pelvis can remain steady.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('CI6baTY','Bottoms-Up','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your legs extended and your arms by your sides.','Bend your knees and bring them toward your chest, keeping your feet off the ground.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('CjETvlw','Roller Seated Single Leg Shoulder Flexor Depressor Retractor','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'roller',array['Take a seat on a flat surface with your legs extended in front of you.','Take hold of the roller with both hands, palms facing down, and place it on your thighs.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('cJgSTmh','Oblique Crunch','waist','abdominals',array['obliques'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands behind your head or cross them over your chest.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('CJwa0vD','Dumbbell Standing Bent Over Single-Arm Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids','back'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in one hand.','Bend forward at the waist, with your spine steady and parallel to the ground.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('CMAxnsG','Clock Push-Up','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids','core'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body in a straight line.','Lower your body toward the ground by bending your elbows, keeping them close to your sides.','Brace the abdomen and glutes so the shoulders, hips and ankles move together.','Bend your elbows to lower your chest while keeping your body in one line.','Keep the head in line with the spine as the elbows bend.','Press back to straight arms, keeping the body line intact.'],0),
('CmEr4pM','Cable Wide-Grip Rear Pulldown Behind Neck','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','rhomboids','rear deltoids'],'cable',array['Set the cable machine so that the pulldown bar is at a height above your head.','Sit on the seat and grab the pulldown bar with a wide overhand grip.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Draw the bar toward the upper back behind your head only as far as the shoulders allow comfortably.','Pull with the elbows rather than leaning far back to move the handle.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('CosupLu','Front Plank with Twist','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body in a straight line from head to toe.','Brace your trunk and glutes to maintain a stable position.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],8),
('cQ19bBP','Rocky Pull-Up Pulldown','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Take your place in front of a pull-up bar with your feet about shoulder width.','Reach up to hold the bar with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('CQHoDm0','Ez-Bar Decline Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'EZ bar',array['Settle onto a decline bench with your head lower than your feet and your feet secured.','Take hold of the ez barbell with palms facing down, hands about shoulder width.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('CqhoytW','Smith Hip Raise','waist','abdominals',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'smith machine',array['Set yourself on the smith machine with your back against the pad and your feet about shoulder width.','Set your hands on the barbell, just beyond shoulder width.','Plant the feet and keep the ribs from flaring as the hips prepare to rise.','Press through the feet and lift your hips until your torso and thighs line up.','Stop when the hips line up with the torso; do not arch higher through the lower back.','Lower the hips steadily and keep the feet planted for the next lift.'],0),
('CuaWCmC','Cable Lateral Pulldown (With Rope Attachment)','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'cable',array['Connect a rope attachment to the cable machine at a high position.','Face the machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Pull the handle down by driving your elbows toward your ribs; keep your torso steady.','Pull with the elbows rather than leaning far back to move the handle.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('cuKYxhu','Standing Pelvic Tilt','back','erector spinae',array['abdominals'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Set your arms at your sides, or set your hands at your waist.','Relax the shoulders and find a comfortable neutral starting position.','Gently roll the pelvis to flatten and release the lower back through a small range.','Use a small range and avoid forcing the lower back into the floor.','Release the tilt gently and repeat without forcing the range.'],0),
('CvPn9WV','Cable Standing Pulldown (With Rope)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms','deltoids'],'cable',array['Connect a rope to the cable machine at the highest setting.','Face the machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Pull the handle down by driving your elbows toward your ribs; keep your torso steady.','Pull with the elbows rather than leaning far back to move the handle.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('cWemPG8','Dumbbell Prone Incline Hammer Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Set the bench to a 45-degree incline.','Position yourself face down on the bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing each other.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl with palms facing each other and elbows near your sides; avoid rocking back.','Keep the palms facing each other and the wrists straight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('d1GgzTU','L-Pull-Up','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Take hold of the pull-up bar with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Hang with your arms straight and your body straight.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('D1xYJAU','Dumbbell Over Bench Wrist Curl','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','brachialis'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with your forearms resting on the bench and your palms facing up, holding a dumbbell in each hand.','Let your wrists to hang over the edge of the bench.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('d5bTEPV','Band Step-Up','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'resistance band',array['Set a band around your thighs, just above your knees.','Face a step or platform with your feet about hip width.','Put the lead foot fully on the platform before shifting your weight onto it.','Step onto the platform and drive through the lead foot to stand tall on it.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
('D5yqP2p','Machine Overhand Triceps Dip','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'leverage machine',array['Set the machine to the appropriate height and secure your body in position.','Hold the handles with palms facing down and position your body so that your arms are straight.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('d7z1Y7V','Exercise Ball Hug','back','erector spinae',array['deltoids','pectorals'],'stability ball',array['Take a seat on the stability ball with your feet planted and your back straight.','Take hold of the stability ball with both hands, hugging it close to your chest.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('d960PgE','Barbell Seated Good Morning','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'barbell',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; a barbell resting on your upper back.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and your chest up.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Push the hips back while keeping the load close and the spine steady.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('D9qe7CM','Pelvic Tilt Into Bridge','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','core'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your arms by your sides with your palms facing down.','Plant the feet and keep the ribs from flaring as the hips prepare to rise.','Tuck the pelvis gently, then push through the feet to raise the hips into a bridge.','Stop when the hips line up with the torso; do not arch higher through the lower back.','Lower the hips steadily and keep the feet planted for the next lift.'],0),
('d9Xaxq6','Cable Russian Twists (On Stability Ball)','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','erector spinae'],'cable',array['Take a seat on a stability ball with your feet planted and your knees bent at a 90-degree angle.','Take hold of the cable handle with both hands and extend your arms straight out in front of you.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('da4cXST','Ez-Bar Close-Grip Bench Press','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'EZ bar',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your back pressed against the bench.','Hold the ez barbell with a close grip, hands about shoulder width, palms facing forward.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('daBmy1Y','Dumbbell Single Leg Deadlift with Stepbox Support','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about hip width, holding a dumbbell in your right hand.','Set your left foot on a stepbox or elevated surface behind you.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Push the hips back while keeping the load close and the spine steady.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('dB07vDu','Single-Arm Bent-Over Cable Lateral Raise','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','trapezius'],'cable',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, facing a cable machine.','Hold the handle with one hand and step back to create tension on the cable.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Raise the arms out to the sides to about shoulder height without leaning or shrugging.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('DB0n8AG','Kettlebell Front Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes slightly turned out.','Take hold of the kettlebell with both hands ahead of your chest, close to your body.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('Db7eEgw','Cable Concentration Extension (On Knee)','upper arms','triceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Take a seat on a bench or chair with your knees bent and feet planted.','Take hold of the cable handle with your right hand and place your elbow on the inside of your right knee.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('dCJnuVq','Medicine Ball Chest Push From 3 Point Stance','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'medicine ball',array['Begin in a 3 point stance with one hand on the medicine ball and the other hand on the ground.','Reach your legs and position your body in a straight line.','Set a firm stance and leave enough clear space for the ball to travel.','Drive the ball away forcefully, using the arms and trunk together; catch or retrieve it before resetting.','Follow through with the whole body while keeping control of the landing or catch.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('dCPESfR','Barbell Standing Bradford Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','upper back'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold the barbell ahead of your shoulders with palms facing down.','Press the barbell overhead, straighten your arms.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('DeDThfG','Seated Glute Stretch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on the ground with your legs extended in front of you.','Before moving, bend your right knee and cross your right ankle over your left thigh.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('DEEqoI2','Posterior Tibialis Stretch','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','quadriceps'],'rope',array['Take a seat on the ground with your legs extended in front of you.','Thread the rope around the ball of your foot and hold the ends of the rope with your hands.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('DFGXwZr','World Greatest Stretch','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes','quadriceps','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a lunge position with your right foot forward and your left foot back.','Set your hands on the ground on either side of your right foot.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('dFSNDOA','Barbell Seated Twist','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','erector spinae'],'barbell',array['Take a seat on a flat bench with your feet planted and your knees bent.','Take a barbell with both hands ahead of your chest, keeping your elbows soft.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the turn smooth instead of throwing the arms across the body.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('dG5Smob','Snatch Pull','upper legs','quadriceps',array['hamstrings','glutes','calves'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and the barbell on the ground in front of you.','Bend your knees and hinge at the hips to lower into a squat position, gripping the barbell with palms facing down.','Brace before the pull and keep the load close to the body.','Drive through the legs and hips, then guide the weight to its receiving position.','Receive the load with the torso braced and feet stable.','Stand tall to finish, then lower the weight under control before the next rep.'],0),
('dG7tG5y','Barbell Shrug','back','trapezius',array['deltoids'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell in front of you with palms facing down.','Keep your arms long and your spine steady throughout the exercise.','Let the arms hang long and keep the head neutral.','Lift your shoulders toward your ears without bending the elbows or rolling the shoulders.','Lift and lower vertically without circling the shoulders.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('DgZQ11d','Ez-Bar Decline Close-Grip Face Press','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'EZ bar',array['Settle onto a decline bench with your head lower than your feet.','Hold the ez barbell with a close grip, palms facing each other.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('DhMl549','Barbell Full Squat (Back Pov)','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves','core'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes slightly turned out.','Rest the bar across the upper back and take a secure grip.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('DIVyqrU','Sphinx','back','erector spinae',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Position yourself face down on the ground with your forearms flat on the floor, elbows directly under your shoulders.','Brace your trunk and lift your chest off the ground, keeping your forearms and toes on the floor.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('dK9394r','Burpee','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves','deltoids','pectorals'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a standing position with your feet about shoulder width.','Before moving, lower your body into a squat position by bending your knees and placing your hands on the floor in front of you.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Move at a repeatable pace, keeping the motion smooth and your breathing steady.','Keep the pattern repeatable as speed increases.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],1),
('DKBwJrL','Band Single-Arm Twisting Seated Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','deltoids'],'resistance band',array['Take a seat on a bench or chair with your feet planted and your back straight.','Take hold of the band with one hand and extend your arm fully in front of you.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('dmgMp3n','Barbell Incline Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'barbell',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Position yourself face down on the bench with your chest against the pad and your feet planted.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('DOoWcnA','Machine Chest Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles with palms facing down and position your elbows at a 90-degree angle.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('DotAgEF','Barbell Reverse-Grip Decline Bench Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Secure the feet on a decline bench, keeping the head below the hips.','Hold the barbell with a reverse grip, just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the palms in the chosen grip without bending the wrists back.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('dPmaUaU','Dumbbell Standing Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['ankles'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand.','Before moving, raise your heels off the ground as high as possible, using your calves.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('DptumMx','Band Close-Grip Pulldown','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'resistance band',array['Connect the band to a high anchor point, such as a pull-up bar or sturdy beam.','Face the anchor point and grab the band with palms facing up, hands about shoulder width.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Pull the handle down by driving your elbows toward your ribs; keep your torso steady.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('DpWMFP5','Cable Seated Overhead Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms','deltoids'],'cable',array['Take a seat on a bench facing the cable machine with your feet planted.','Hold the cable attachment with palms facing up, and your hands about shoulder width.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
