('hCjGsRQ','Power Point Plank','waist','abdominals',array['deltoids','triceps','glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body in a straight line from head to toe.','Brace your trunk and squeeze your glutes to maintain a stable position.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],0),
('HDYiZcY','Dumbbell Cross Body Hammer Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body.','Hold your elbows near your torso and your upper arms stationary.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl each weight across the torso toward the opposite shoulder, keeping the palm facing inward.','Keep the palms facing each other and the wrists straight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('HEJ6DIX','Cable Kickback','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'cable',array['Face the cable machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Take hold of the cable handle with your right hand and step back to create tension in the cable.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Hold the upper arm beside your torso and straighten the elbow behind you.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('hfmQ0Tz','Smith Standing Back Wrist Curl','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','triceps'],'smith machine',array['Face the smith machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Hold the barbell with palms facing down, hands about shoulder width.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('HfqciZF','Straddle Maltese','waist','abdominals',array['deltoids','pectorals'],'bodyweight',array['Begin by hanging from a pair of rings with your arms straight and your body in a straight line.','Move your legs wide apart, forming a straddle position.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],0),
('Hgs6Nl1','Seated Leg Raise','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on a flat bench with your back straight and your feet planted.','Set your hands on the sides of the bench for support.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Slow the legs before they pull the lower back out of position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('hHy8tQG','Cable Single-Arm Fly on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'cable',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with your feet planted and your back straight.','Take a cable handle in one hand and extend your arm out to the side, parallel to the ground.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('HIgYKAB','Seated Wide Angle Pose Sequence','upper legs','hamstrings',array['quadriceps','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on the ground with your legs extended in a wide angle.','Pull your toes toward you and engage your quadriceps.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('Hj4FOCd','Barbell Decline Wide-Grip Pullover','back','latissimus dorsi',array['triceps','pectorals'],'barbell',array['Settle onto a decline bench with your head lower than your hips and your feet secured.','Take a barbell with a wide grip and extend your arms straight above your chest.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ribs down as the arms travel overhead.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('HJ63mSO','Barbell Lying Close-Grip Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'barbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your head at the end of the bench.','Hold the barbell with a close grip, hands about shoulder width, palms facing up.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('HjdqmZa','Single-Arm Chin-Up','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Face the pull-up bar from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Reach up to hold the bar with palms facing up, with one hand gripping the bar and the other hand holding your wrist for support.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('hl8DUh8','Barbell Decline Wide-Grip Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Secure the feet on a decline bench, keeping the head below the hips.','Hold the barbell with a wide grip, just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('hMEptv0','Barbell Decline Bent Arm Pullover','back','latissimus dorsi',array['triceps','pectorals'],'barbell',array['Get onto a decline bench with your head lower than your hips and your feet secured.','Take a barbell with a pronated grip (palms turned away from you) and extend your arms straight above your chest.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ribs down as the arms travel overhead.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('HMzLjXx','Weighted Pull-Up','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'weighted',array['Take hold of the pull-up bar with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Suspend yourself from the bar with your arms straight and your body straight.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('hnOYgH3','Ez-Bar JM Bench Press','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'EZ bar',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your back pressed against the bench.','Hold the ez barbell with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('hoXt6wv','Left Hook (Boxing)','shoulders','deltoids',array['biceps','triceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Keep the left hand up to protect your face and your right hand by your chin.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Pivot through the hips and feet as the left arm travels across at chest height.','Keep the pattern repeatable as speed increases.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],0),
('HPlPoQA','Cable Hammer Curl (With Rope)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Stand upright with your feet about shoulder width and a slight bend in your knees.','Take hold of the cable rope attachment with palms facing up, palms facing each other, and your arms straight.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl with palms facing each other and elbows near your sides; avoid rocking back.','Keep the palms facing each other and the wrists straight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('hq2hyDH','Dumbbell Standing Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand upright with your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing forward.','Rest the back of your upper arms against the preacher bench or an incline bench, with your elbows soft.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('hrrS0Ed','Dumbbell Seated Lateral Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; a dumbbell in each hand, resting on your thighs.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and core engaged.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Raise the arms out to the sides to about shoulder height without leaning or shrugging.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
