('IMRsOCn','Squat Jerk','upper legs','quadriceps',array['glutes','hamstrings','calves','core'],'barbell',array['Start with the barbell resting on your shoulders, with your feet about shoulder width.','Before moving, lower your body into a squat position, keeping your chest up and your knees tracking over your toes.','Brace before the pull and keep the load close to the body.','Drive through the legs and hips, then guide the weight to its receiving position.','Receive the load with the torso braced and feet stable.','Stand tall to finish, then lower the weight under control before the next rep.'],0),
('iny3m5y','Dead Bug','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','erector spinae'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your arms extended toward the ceiling.','Before moving, bend your knees and lift your legs off the ground, creating a 90-degree angle at your hips and knees.','Brace the trunk lightly before moving a limb.','Move the working arm or leg while keeping the trunk steady and the breathing even.','Keep the pelvis from rocking as the arm or leg moves.','Reset your posture before changing sides or beginning the next rep.'],0),
('Ion0XWz','Dumbbell Lying on Floor Rear Delt Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','rhomboids'],'dumbbell',array['Position yourself face down on the floor with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing each other.','Reach your arms straight out in front of you, keeping a slight bend in your elbows.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the arms out and back with soft elbows, letting the rear shoulders do the work.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('ioTf098','Cable Overhead Curl on Exercise Ball','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms','deltoids'],'cable',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball and hold the cable handle with palms facing up.','Reach your arms fully overhead, keeping your elbows close to your ears.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('iPm26QU','Box Jump Down with Single-Leg Stabilization','lower legs','calves',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Take your place in front of a box or platform with your feet about shoulder width.','Before moving, bend your knees and jump onto the box, landing softly with one foot on the box and the other foot hanging off the edge.','Bend the hips and knees slightly to load the jump.','Load the legs with a small bend, then drive through the floor and land softly.','Keep the pelvis level as the supporting leg does the work.','Absorb the landing through the hips and knees before repeating; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('IpONWYv','Dumbbell Side Bend','waist','abdominals',array['obliques'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in one hand, letting it hang down by your side.','With your back straight and your core engaged, With control bend sideways at the waist toward the opposite side of the dumbbell, lowering the weight as far as you comfortably can.','Stand or sit tall with the pelvis facing forward.','Bend sideways through the waist without twisting or letting the hips shift.','Let the side of the trunk work; do not twist or shift the hips.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('Iptlv6x','Dumbbell Upright Row (Back Pov)','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','biceps'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with palms facing down.','Let the dumbbells hang ahead of your thighs, with your arms straight and your palms facing your body.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('ipvgBnC','Barbell Seated Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings'],'barbell',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; a barbell resting on your thighs.','Set the balls of your feet on a raised platform, such as a block or step.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('iQ241UP','Half Sit-Up','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands behind your head with your elbows pointing outwards.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('isAAZWA','Side-To-Side Chin','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Hold a pull-up bar with palms facing down, hands just beyond shoulder width.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('isofgzg','Roller Back Stretch','back','erector spinae',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'roller',array['Begin by sitting on the ground with your legs extended in front of you.','Set the roller perpendicular to your body, just below your glutes.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('IvV6C9M','Dumbbell Over Bench Single-Arm Neutral Wrist Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with a dumbbell in one hand and your arm extended over the bench, palm facing up.','Keep your upper arm stationary and curl the dumbbell toward your shoulder, keeping your wrist in a neutral position.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('IwX5NqK','Cable Reverse Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Set the cable machine so that the preacher curl pad is at chest height.','Take a seat on the preacher curl bench and place your upper arms on the pad, with your palms facing down and your elbows straight.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('iYzB0Cz','Barbell Full Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves','core'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes slightly turned out.','Rest the bar across the upper back and take a secure grip.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],46),
('izMnLqz','Dumbbell Alternate Side Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','core'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand at shoulder height.','Before moving, press one dumbbell overhead while keeping the other dumbbell at shoulder height.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('iZop9xO','Barbell Lying Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'barbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your head at the end of the bench.','Take hold of the barbell with palms facing down, hands about shoulder width, and extend your arms straight up over your chest.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('IZVHb27','Walking Lunge','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Step forward with your right leg, lowering your body into a lunge position.','Set your stance wide enough to balance before bending either knee.','Step into the movement and bend both knees, keeping your front foot planted.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
('J60bN17','Assisted Triceps Dip (Kneeling)','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'leverage machine',array['Set the machine to your desired weight and height.','Get down on the pad facing the machine, with your hands gripping the handles.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('J6Dx1Mu','Barbell Close-Grip Bench Press','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your feet planted and your back pressed against the bench.','Hold the barbell with a close grip, slightly narrower than about shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('j74M6Zn','Exercise Ball on the Wall Calf Raise (Tennis Ball Between Knees)','lower legs','calves',array['quadriceps','hamstrings'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your back against a wall and place an exercise ball between your lower back and the wall.','Set your feet about shoulder width and slightly in front of you.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
