('K3dIO25','Dumbbell Lying Single-Arm Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your back supported and feet planted.','Take a dumbbell in one hand with your palm facing toward your feet.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('k5IpyHg','Dumbbell Single-Arm Concentration Curl (On Stability Ball)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a stability ball with your feet planted and your knees bent at a 90-degree angle.','Take a dumbbell in one hand with your palm facing up and your arm extended down toward the floor.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('K5xgdvI','Reclining Big Toe Pose with Rope','upper legs','hamstrings',array['calves','glutes'],'rope',array['Settle onto your back with your legs extended and your arms by your sides.','Thread the rope around the ball of your right foot and hold the ends of the rope with your hands.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('k6tUeqS','Band Underhand Pulldown','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'resistance band',array['Connect the band to a high anchor point, such as a pull-up bar or sturdy beam.','Face the anchor point from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Pull the handle down by driving your elbows toward your ribs; keep your torso steady.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('K9VL0Jq','Lunge with Twist','waist','abdominals',array['quadriceps','glutes','hamstrings'],'bodyweight',array['Begin by standing with your feet about shoulder width.','Step forward with your right foot, lowering your body into a lunge position.','Set your stance wide enough to balance before bending either knee.','Step into the movement and bend both knees, keeping your front foot planted.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
('Kal9cQQ','Kettlebell Advanced Windmill','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','deltoids'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet wider than about shoulder width, toes pointing slightly outward.','Take a kettlebell in your right hand, with your arm extended overhead and your palm facing forward.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the turn smooth instead of throwing the arms across the body.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('KCBKjma','Band Jack Knife Sit-Up','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'resistance band',array['Settle onto your back with your legs straight and your arms extended overhead, holding the band.','Tighten your midsection and lift your legs and upper body simultaneously, bringing your hands toward your feet.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('kesXOpB','Cable Decline Seated Wide-Grip Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'cable',array['Take a seat on the decline bench facing the cable machine with your feet securely placed on the footrests.','Hold the cable attachment with a wide overhand grip, palms facing down.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('KgI0tqW','Barbell Sumo Deadlift','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps','erector spinae'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet wider than about shoulder width, toes pointing outwards.','Set a barbell on the ground in front of you, centered between your feet.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Push the hips back while keeping the load close and the spine steady.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('KHGNa16','Cable Decline Single-Arm Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'cable',array['Set the cable machine to a decline position.','Face away from the machine and grab the handle with one hand.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('KhHJ338','Push-Up to Side Plank','waist','abdominals',array['deltoids','pectorals','triceps'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a push-up position with your hands about shoulder width and your body in a straight line.','Lower your body toward the ground by bending your elbows, keeping your core engaged.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],0),
