('LHWF7us','Kettlebell Hang Clean','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes','quadriceps','calves'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a kettlebell ahead of your thighs.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady.','Brace before the pull and keep the load close to the body.','Drive through the legs and hips, then guide the weight to its receiving position.','Receive the load with the torso braced and feet stable.','Stand tall to finish, then lower the weight under control before the next rep.'],0),
('lI7easp','Dumbbell Pullover Hip Extension on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids','core'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with your feet planted and the dumbbell resting on your thighs.','With control walk your feet forward, rolling the exercise ball down your back until your head, neck, and upper back are supported on the ball.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('LIGZSTA','Dumbbell Single-Arm Prone Hammer Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Position yourself face down on a flat bench with a dumbbell in one hand, palm facing your body and arm straight.','Keep your upper arm stationary and curl the dumbbell toward your shoulder, contracting your biceps.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl with palms facing each other and elbows near your sides; avoid rocking back.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('LIlE5Tn','Jump Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width.','Before moving, lower your body into a squat position by bending your knees and pushing your hips back.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('lJJ7Yq8','Cable Lying Fly','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'cable',array['Connect the handles to the cables and Lie back on the bench with your feet planted.','Take hold of the handles with your palms facing each other and your arms extended straight above your chest.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep the elbow angle nearly unchanged through the arc.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load.'],0),
('LkoAWAE','Elbow Dips','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on the edge of a bench or chair with your hands gripping the edge next to your hips.','Move your hips forward off the bench and straighten your legs, keeping your heels on the ground.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('LL1UiTX','Dumbbell Incline Single-Arm Hammer Press','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids','pectorals'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an incline bench with a dumbbell in one hand, resting on your thigh.','Recline on the bench and use your thigh to help raise the dumbbell to shoulder height.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('LLNh6q5','Dumbbell Incline Single-Arm Fly on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with a dumbbell in one hand.','Step your feet forward and roll your body down until your head, neck, and upper back are supported on the ball.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
