('Ln9iTbU','Barbell Rear Delt Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','rhomboids'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell with palms facing down.','Bend your knees slightly and hinge forward at the hips, with your spine steady.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the arms out and back with soft elbows, letting the rear shoulders do the work.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('LNE3wfo','Single Leg Platform Slide','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes','quadriceps'],'bodyweight',array['Begin by standing with one foot on a platform or slide board.','Before moving, bend your knee slightly and slide the foot on the platform backward, extending your leg.','Set your stance wide enough to balance before bending either knee.','Step into the movement and bend both knees, keeping your front foot planted.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
