('mym4hJo','Dumbbell Lying Pronation','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a bench with your chest facing down and your arms extended straight down, holding a dumbbell in each hand.','Before moving, rotate your palms so they are facing up.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('Mz6lLcW','Dumbbell Lunge with Biceps Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['quadriceps','hamstrings'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing forward.','Step forward with your right foot, lowering your body into a lunge position. Your right knee should be bent at a 90-degree angle and your left knee should be hovering just above the ground.','Set your stance wide enough to balance before bending either knee.','Step into the movement and bend both knees, keeping your front foot planted.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],0),
('MzNnwx9','Smith Back Shrug','back','trapezius',array['deltoids'],'smith machine',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Hold the barbell with palms facing down, hands just beyond shoulder width.','Let the arms hang long and keep the head neutral.','Lift your shoulders toward your ears without bending the elbows or rolling the shoulders.','Lift and lower vertically without circling the shoulders.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('n5cWCsI','Dumbbell Single-Arm Lateral Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in one hand with your palm facing your body.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and your core engaged throughout the exercise.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Raise the arms out to the sides to about shoulder height without leaning or shrugging.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('NAgVB3t','Wheel Rollout','waist','abdominals',array['erector spinae'],'ab wheel',array['Get down on the floor and place the wheel roller in front of you.','Set your hands on the handles of the wheel roller and extend your arms straight out in front of you.','Tighten the abdomen and keep the pelvis tucked before the arms reach away.','Reach the arms away while keeping your ribs and pelvis aligned; stop before the lower back sags.','Stop reaching when the lower back starts to sag.','Pull back to the start through your shoulders and abdominals, keeping the same body line.'],0),
('NAkmgdx','Arms Overhead Full Sit-Up','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','erector spinae'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Reach your arms overhead, keeping them straight.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('nAuHPcD','Dumbbell Single-Arm Triceps Extension (On Bench)','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with your back straight and feet planted.','Take a dumbbell in one hand and place your other hand on the bench for support.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('NbVPDMW','Dumbbell Biceps Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing forward and arms straight.','With your upper arms stationary, exhale and curl the weights while contracting your biceps.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],39),
('nCU1Ekp','Reverse Crunch','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your arms extended along your sides.','Before moving, bend your knees and lift your feet off the ground, bringing your thighs perpendicular to the floor.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('NdIb5Z1','Barbell Standing Wide-Grip Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms','deltoids'],'barbell',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell with palms facing down, hands wider than about shoulder width.','Keep the barbell hanging at arm''s length ahead of your thighs, with your palms turned away from your body.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('nDK1HJ0','Ez-Bar Lying Bent Arms Pullover','back','latissimus dorsi',array['triceps','pectorals'],'EZ bar',array['Settle onto a bench with your head at one end and your feet on the floor.','Take hold of the EZ barbell with a pronated grip (palms turned away from you) and your hands about shoulder width.','Set the ribs down and keep a small elbow bend before lowering the weight.','Lower the weight in an arc behind your head until you feel a comfortable shoulder stretch.','Keep the ribs down as the arms travel overhead.','Pull the weight back over the chest along the same arc, without lifting the ribs.'],0),
('neonEDL','Floor Fly (With Barbell)','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'barbell',array['Settle onto your back on the floor with your knees bent and feet planted.','Take a barbell with palms facing down, arms extended straight up over your chest.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep the elbow angle nearly unchanged through the arc.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load.'],0),
('nFc4FyV','Dumbbell Biceps Curl Reverse','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing down and arms straight.','With your upper arms stationary, exhale and curl the weights while contracting your biceps.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl the weight with your palms facing down, keeping the elbows close and torso still.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('NfP83rA','Dumbbell Lying Alternate Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing each other.','Reach your arms straight up over your chest, keeping a slight bend in your elbows.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('nFUwqG6','Smith Rear Delt Row','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','rhomboids','biceps'],'smith machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('ngPpyRS','Barbell Seated Behind Head Military Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','upper back'],'barbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with your back straight and feet planted.','Take hold of the barbell with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('Nh3mvOO','Dumbbell Reverse-Grip Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and knees soft.','Take a dumbbell in each hand with palms facing down, palms facing your body.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep the palms in the chosen grip without bending the wrists back.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('nIR4Rwl','Cable Seated Chest Press','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'cable',array['Set the seat height and cable handles to a comfortable position.','Take a seat on the bench with your back straight and feet planted.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('niXESDw','Dumbbell Biceps Curl Squat','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing forward.','With your back straight and your elbows close to your sides, exhale and curl the dumbbells up toward your shoulders.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('NJzBsGJ','Dumbbell Shrug','back','trapezius',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing your body.','Maintain straight arms and let the dumbbells hang by your sides.','Let the arms hang long and keep the head neutral.','Lift your shoulders toward your ears without bending the elbows or rolling the shoulders.','Lift and lower vertically without circling the shoulders.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],18),
('NKJ8o6x','Pelvic Tilt','waist','abdominals',array['erector spinae'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands by your sides.','Relax the shoulders and find a comfortable neutral starting position.','Gently roll the pelvis to flatten and release the lower back through a small range.','Use a small range and avoid forcing the lower back into the floor.','Release the tilt gently and repeat without forcing the range.'],0),
('NL6YBwN','Dumbbell Decline Single-Arm Fly','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Get onto a decline bench with a dumbbell in one hand, resting it on your thigh.','Use your thigh to help raise the dumbbell, lift it up to shoulder width with your palm facing your torso.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('NlfIbzq','Dumbbell Alternate Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a preacher bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing up.','Set your upper arms on the pad of the preacher bench, letting your arms to fully extend.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('nlJsbkW','Dumbbell Biceps Curl (With Arm Blaster)','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing forward.','Hold your elbows near your torso and your upper arms stationary.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('NN8nSNT','Cable Rope High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'cable',array['Connect a rope to a high pulley and adjust the weight accordingly.','Face the away from the pulley machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms pointed upward and extend at the elbows without flaring the ribs.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('nnmCTLN','Machine Kneeling Leg Curl','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes'],'leverage machine',array['Set the machine to fit your body and select the desired weight.','Get down on the machine facing downwards, with your knees resting on the pad and your feet secured under the footpads.','Line the knees up with the machine or bench edge before starting the curl.','Bend your knees to draw the pad toward you without lifting your hips from the support.','Keep the hips still while the knees bend.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('NNoHCEA','Smith Full Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'smith machine',array['Prepare the smith machine with the barbell at shoulder height.','Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes slightly turned out.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('nqs5HGV','Single Leg Squat (Pistol)','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and arms extended in front of you.','Before moving, lift your right foot off the ground and extend it forward.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Extend the free leg ahead of you as you squat on the standing leg, keeping its heel grounded.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('Nu7jqFE','Band Seated Straight Back Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','deltoids'],'resistance band',array['Take a seat on the floor with your legs extended and loop the resistance band around your feet.','Take hold of the ends of the resistance band with your hands, palms facing each other.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('nuBF9MO','Hanging Pike','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Suspend yourself from a pull-up bar with your arms straight and your palms turned away from you.','Brace your trunk and lift your legs up toward the bar, keeping them straight.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Slow the legs before they pull the lower back out of position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('nUwVh7b','Dumbbell Deadlift','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes pointing forward.','Take a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing your body, arms extended downwards.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Push the hips back while keeping the load close and the spine steady.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('NvfE43H','Cable Concentration Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Take a seat on a bench or chair with your feet planted and your knees soft.','Take hold of the cable handle with palms facing up and rest your elbow against the inside of your thigh.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('nxW6BkN','Dumbbell Incline Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand, resting on your thighs.','Recline on the bench and raise the dumbbells to shoulder height, palms facing forward.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the weights away from your torso to about shoulder height, keeping the elbows softly bent.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('NZ5Qqkz','Reverse Dip','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Set yourself between two parallel bars with your arms straight and your body straight.','Before moving, lower your body by bending your elbows until your upper arms are parallel to the ground.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('nZZZy9m','Machine High Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','rear deltoids'],'leverage machine',array['Set the seat height and foot platform to a comfortable position.','Take a seat on the machine with your chest against the pad and your feet flat on the foot platform.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('o1HGDSq','Exercise Ball Back Extension with Hands Behind Head','back','erector spinae',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'stability ball',array['Set the stability ball on the ground and Position yourself face down on top of it with your hips resting on the ball.','Set your feet against a wall or other stable surface for support.','Secure the hips and feet on the support before lifting.','Raise your torso or legs until they line up with your body, without arching sharply at the lower back.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('o1ntciW','Olympic Barbell Hammer Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'olympic barbell',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold an Olympic barbell with palms facing down.','Keep the barbell hanging at arm''s length ahead of your thighs, with your palms facing your body.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Curl with palms facing each other and elbows near your sides; avoid rocking back.','Keep the palms facing each other and the wrists straight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('O2K9Vb5','Wide-Grip Chest Dip on High Parallel Bars','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Set yourself on the parallel bars with your arms straight and your body suspended in the air.','Tip forward slightly and lower your body by bending your elbows until your chest is just above the bars.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('O4oIqQD','Bodyweight Standing Single-Arm Row (With Towel)','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, knees soft, and hold a towel with one hand.','Bend forward at the hips, with your spine steady and your core engaged.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('o5Jsk92','Dumbbell Single-Arm Bench Fly','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a flat bench with a dumbbell in one hand, resting it on top of your thigh.','Recline on the bench, keeping the dumbbell pressed against your thigh.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('o8aOcrz','Smith Machine Incline Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'smith machine',array['Set the seat of the smith machine so that the bar is at shoulder height.','Take a seat on the bench with your back against the pad and your feet planted.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('O8Aq69u','Dumbbell Reverse Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a preacher bench with your upper arms resting on the pad and your chest against the support.','Take a dumbbell in each hand with palms facing up.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('O8o7q4d','Dumbbell Press on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with your feet planted and dumbbells in each hand, resting on your thighs.','With control walk your feet forward, rolling the exercise ball until your lower back is supported on the ball and your knees are at a 90-degree angle.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('O95afRA','Monster Walk','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps'],'bodyweight',array['Set a resistance band around your ankles.','Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and slightly bend your knees.','Stand tall with the load secure and the shoulders level.','Walk at a controlled pace, keeping your shoulders level and your steps even.','Keep steps even and avoid leaning away from the load.','Stop before posture breaks down, set the load down safely, and reset for the next walk.'],0),
('OaE7CpD','Kettlebell Double Windmill','waist','abdominals',array['deltoids','hamstrings'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a kettlebell in your right hand.','Reach your right arm overhead, keeping your eyes on the kettlebell.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the turn smooth instead of throwing the arms across the body.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
