('obe5LMq','Band Side Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'resistance band',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold the band with both hands, palms facing down.','Reach your arms straight out to the sides, keeping them parallel to the ground.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('ocYc6Db','Dumbbell Standing Single-Arm Palm in Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','core'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in one hand at shoulder height with your palm facing inwards.','Brace your trunk and Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('OeL23VY','Dumbbell Seated Biceps Curl to Shoulder Press','upper arms','biceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench with your back straight and feet planted.','Take a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing forward and arms straight.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('oHg8eop','Medicine Ball Overhead Slam','back','upper back',array['deltoids','core'],'medicine ball',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a medicine ball with both hands above your head.','Brace your trunk and Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position.','Set a firm stance and leave enough clear space for the ball to travel.','Drive the ball away forcefully, using the arms and trunk together; catch or retrieve it before resetting.','Follow through with the whole body while keeping control of the landing or catch.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('oHsrypV','Machine Seated Hip Adduction','upper legs','adductors',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Set your feet on the footrests and Hold the handles for stability.','Square the pelvis before moving the working leg.','Draw the working leg inward against resistance without leaning sideways.','Move only as far as the pelvis can remain steady.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('OIFMAp1','Machine Single-Arm Lateral High Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','deltoids'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handle with one hand and Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('oLrKqDH','Run','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Begin by standing upright with your feet about hip width.','Brace your trunk and keep your upper body relaxed.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Move at a repeatable pace, keeping the motion smooth and your breathing steady.','Keep the pattern repeatable as speed increases.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],5),
('OM46QHm','Cable Pull Through (With Rope)','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'cable',array['Stand facing away from the low pulley with the rope passing between your legs.','Take hold of the rope attachment with both hands and step forward, creating tension in the cable.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Push the hips back while keeping the load close and the spine steady.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('OmQ8w0p','Cable Palm Rotational Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'cable',array['Connect a handle to a cable machine at waist height.','Face the machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('oMypNrz','Roller Hip Stretch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps'],'roller',array['Begin by sitting on the ground with your legs extended in front of you.','Set the roller under your glutes, just above your knees.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('oom75KC','Dumbbell Straight-Leg Deadlift','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with palms facing down.','With your back straight and your core engaged, hinge at the hips and lower the dumbbells toward the ground, letting your torso to lean forward.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Send your hips back with a soft knee bend, lowering the load close to your legs until the hamstrings stretch.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('OPqShYN','Machine Hip Extension','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings'],'leverage machine',array['Set the machine to fit your body and sit on it with your back against the backrest.','Set your feet on the footrests and grip the handles for stability.','Plant the feet and keep the ribs from flaring as the hips prepare to rise.','Press through the feet and lift your hips until your torso and thighs line up.','Stop when the hips line up with the torso; do not arch higher through the lower back.','Lower the hips steadily and keep the feet planted for the next lift.'],0),
('OQ1otBN','Cable Crossover Lateral Pulldown','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','rhomboids','rear deltoids'],'cable',array['Connect a cable handle to each side of a cable machine at shoulder height.','Take your place in the middle of the machine with your feet about shoulder width.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','Bring the handles across the front of your chest in a broad arc, keeping a slight elbow bend.','Keep the elbow angle nearly unchanged through the arc.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load.'],0),
('oR7O9LW','Barbell Squat (On Knees)','upper legs','quadriceps',array['glutes','hamstrings','calves'],'barbell',array['Begin by kneeling on the ground with your knees about hip width and your toes pointing forward.','Set a barbell across your shoulders, gripping it with palms facing down and your hands just beyond shoulder width.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('OrETs32','Reverse Hyper on Flat Bench','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'bodyweight',array['Position yourself face down on a flat bench with your hips at the edge and your legs hanging off the bench.','Use the bench for stability.','Secure the hips and feet on the support before lifting.','Raise your torso or legs until they line up with your body, without arching sharply at the lower back.','Finish in a straight body line, before the lower back overarches.','Bring the weight or body back to its starting position without rushing.'],0),
('oROuvrX','Machine Unilateral Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'leverage machine',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles with palms facing down and Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('osdXT3K','Kettlebell Single-Arm Push Press','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','core'],'kettlebell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a kettlebell in one hand at shoulder level.','Bend your knees slightly and Brace your trunk.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('OTgkHwR','Dumbbell Decline Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a decline bench with your head lower than your feet and hold a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing each other.','Reach your arms fully, keeping your elbows close to your head.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('otqIxU4','Cable Lying Biceps Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Connect a straight bar to a low pulley cable machine.','Lie face up on a flat bench with your feet planted.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('OUQ0ZyW','Smith Shrug','back','trapezius',array['deltoids'],'smith machine',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your knees soft.','Hold the barbell with palms facing down, hands just beyond shoulder width.','Let the arms hang long and keep the head neutral.','Lift your shoulders toward your ears without bending the elbows or rolling the shoulders.','Lift and lower vertically without circling the shoulders.','Return along the same path at a controlled pace.'],0),
('OVIKwsd','Dumbbell Incline Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing inwards.','Reach your arms fully overhead, keeping your elbows close to your head.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
('OVLmUuL','Dumbbell Incline Palm-In Press','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Angle the bench to roughly 45 degrees.','Take a seat on the bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing each other.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep the wrists stacked and use a shoulder path that feels natural.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again.'],0),
('OVTZ65k','Ez-Barbell Standing Wide-Grip Biceps Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'EZ bar',array['Stand tall with your feet about shoulder width and hold the ez barbell with palms facing up, hands wider than about shoulder width.','Hold your elbows near your torso and your upper arms stationary throughout the movement.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
('OxJk1fg','Cable Triceps Pushdown (V-Bar) (With Arm Blaster)','upper arms','triceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Connect a v-bar attachment to the cable machine at the highest setting.','Face the cable machine from a stable stance with feet about shoulder width.','Stand far enough from the stack for the cable to stay taut.','Keep your elbows near your ribs and straighten your arms against the cable.','Keep the elbows close to the body instead of letting the shoulders swing.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('OYFhXVD','Wide-Grip Rear Pull-Up','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'bodyweight',array['Take hold of the pull-up bar with a wide overhand grip, hands just beyond shoulder width.','Suspend yourself from the bar with your arms straight and your body straight.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull up with control, keeping the head neutral and the elbows moving down beside the torso.','Avoid swinging the legs to clear the bar.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('OyoZ3Pu','Leg Pull in Flat Bench','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors','erector spinae'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on a flat bench with your legs extended straight out in front of you.','Set your hands on the bench beside your hips for support.','Brace the abdomen and keep the shoulders anchored to the support.','Lift your legs by bracing your trunk and moving at the hips rather than swinging.','Slow the legs before they pull the lower back out of position.','Lower the legs slowly without swinging or losing your trunk position.'],0),
('oZjMu1t','Tire Flip','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps','core'],'tire',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, facing the tire.','Before moving, bend your knees and hinge at the hips, lowering into a squat position.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Push the hips back while keeping the load close and the spine steady.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('P14Dz9D','Cable Single-Arm Incline Fly on Exercise Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'cable',array['Take a seat on an exercise ball with your feet planted and your back against an incline bench.','Take a cable handle in one hand with your arm extended and palm facing inward.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('p195zsJ','Two Toe Touch','back','erector spinae',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and your arms extended out to the sides.','Bend forward at the waist, with your spine steady and your knees soft.','Soften the knees and let the hips start the fold.','Fold forward from the hips and let your hands travel toward your feet without forcing the reach.','Keep the movement controlled throughout the range.','Hold briefly at a comfortable depth, then rise by extending the hips.'],0),
('P2lNrGL','Cable Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Set the cable machine so that the preacher curl pad is at chest height.','Take a seat on the preacher curl bench and place your upper arms on the pad, gripping the cable attachment with palms facing up.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl the weight while your upper arms stay in contact with the pad.','Keep the torso quiet and let the elbow bend lift the weight.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still.'],0),
