('r1XNRYB','Band Assisted Pull-Up','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'resistance band',array['Connect the band to a pull-up bar or sturdy anchor point.','Step onto the band and grip the bar with your palms turned away from you, hands just beyond shoulder width.','Begin from a controlled hang with the shoulders active rather than slack.','Pull your elbows down and bring your upper chest toward the bar without kicking your legs.','Control the band on the way back instead of letting it snap you into position.','Lower to long arms without dropping suddenly from the top.'],0),
('r29jP7S','Dumbbell Seated Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a bench or chair with your feet planted and a dumbbell resting on your thighs.','Set the balls of your feet on a raised surface such as a step or block, with your heels hanging off the edge.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('r5DgrW9','Dumbbell Supported Squat','upper legs','quadriceps',array['glutes','hamstrings','calves'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand at your sides.','With your chest up and core engaged, With control lower your body down by bending your knees and pushing your hips back.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('R5swFnc','Cambered Bar Lying Row','back','upper back',array['biceps','forearms'],'barbell',array['Prepare a barbell on the floor and Position yourself face down on a bench with your chest just off the edge.','Reach down and grab the barbell with palms facing down, just beyond shoulder width.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('r7cT9YD','Assisted Motion Russian Twist','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','erector spinae'],'medicine ball',array['Take a seat on the ground with your knees bent and feet planted.','Take hold of the medicine ball with both hands ahead of your chest.','Set the pelvis and make the turn through the rib cage.','Turn through the torso while the hips and lower body stay as steady as the setup allows.','Keep the turn smooth instead of throwing the arms across the body.','Return through center before turning to the other side.'],0),
('rbu5UUb','Cross Body Crunch','waist','abdominals',array['obliques'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Set your hands behind your head with your elbows pointing outwards.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('rDAiRf9','Dumbbell Incline Single-Arm Press','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on an incline bench with a dumbbell in one hand, resting on your thigh.','Recline on the bench and position the dumbbell at shoulder level, palm facing forward.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('reFHapa','Dumbbell Decline Twist Fly','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'dumbbell',array['Get onto a decline bench with your head lower than your hips.','Take a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing each other and your arms extended straight up over your chest.','Keep a soft elbow bend and set the shoulders before moving the arms.','With a soft bend in the elbows, sweep your arms together in a wide arc.','Keep the elbow angle nearly unchanged through the arc.','Open the arms back along the same arc without dropping the load.'],0),
('REGM1dE','Dumbbell Single-Arm Decline Chest Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto a decline bench with a dumbbell in one hand, resting on your chest.','Set your feet planted and keep your back pressed against the bench.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('rEhi2o5','Dumbbell Lying Supination on Floor','lower arms','forearms',array['biceps','deltoids'],'dumbbell',array['Settle onto your back on the floor with your legs extended and your arms by your sides, holding a dumbbell in each hand.','Before moving, rotate your palms to face up, keeping your elbows close to your sides.','Keep the elbows relaxed so the small muscles of the hand or forearm take the load.','Move through the wrists or fingers while the forearms stay supported and still.','Use a small, smooth range without swinging the elbows.','Ease back to the start without letting the load fall from your hands.'],0),
('REXmfVC','Sledge Hammer','waist','abdominals',array['forearms','deltoids'],'hammer',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold the sledge hammer with both hands.','Brace your trunk and Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Swing the hammer down with a coordinated hip turn, then reset your grip and stance.','Keep the palms facing each other and the wrists straight.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],0),
('rg59QCH','Kettlebell Single-Arm Floor Press','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'kettlebell',array['Settle onto your back on the floor with your knees bent and feet planted.','Take hold of the kettlebell in one hand with your palm facing toward your feet and your arm extended straight up toward the ceiling.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('RgJDRR1','Barbell Wide-Grip Upright Row','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','biceps'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a barbell with palms facing down, hands wider than about shoulder width.','Keep the barbell hanging ahead of your thighs, arms straight.','Set the torso and allow the arms to reach forward without rounding excessively.','Draw your elbows back and bring the handle or weight toward your torso.','Bring the elbows back without jerking the torso.','Reach the arms forward again without letting the torso lurch.'],0),
('RGLscZM','Smith Low Bar Squat','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'smith machine',array['Prepare the smith machine with the barbell at a height that allows you to comfortably rest it on your upper back.','Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, toes slightly turned outwards.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('rGwhJ5o','Barbell Standing Leg Calf Raise','lower legs','calves',array['hamstrings','glutes'],'barbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and place a barbell across your upper back.','Before moving, raise your heels off the ground as high as possible, using your calves.','Let the ankles move freely while the rest of the body stays quiet.','Rise through the balls of your feet, lifting the heels as high as you can without rocking.','Pause at the top without rolling the ankles outward.','Lower the heels at a measured pace before rising again.'],0),
('RJa4tCo','Battling Ropes','shoulders','deltoids',array['forearms','core'],'rope',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and knees soft.','Keep one end of the rope in each hand, with your palms facing each other.','Start at a pace that lets the feet and arms move in sync.','Move at a repeatable pace, keeping the motion smooth and your breathing steady.','Keep the pattern repeatable as speed increases.','Keep the rhythm for the planned interval, slowing if your form starts to slip.'],0),
('RJgzwny','Mountain Climber','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['core','deltoids','triceps'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body in a straight line.','Brace your trunk and bring your right knee toward your chest, then quickly switch and bring your left knee toward your chest.','Brace the trunk lightly before moving a limb.','Move the working arm or leg while keeping the trunk steady and the breathing even.','Keep the pelvis from rocking as the arm or leg moves.','Reset your posture before changing sides or beginning the next rep.'],0),
('rjiM4L3','Walking on Incline Treadmill','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'leverage machine',array['Set the incline level on the treadmill to your desired intensity.','Step onto the treadmill with your feet about shoulder width.','Stand tall with the load secure and the shoulders level.','Walk at a controlled pace, keeping your shoulders level and your steps even.','Keep steps even and avoid leaning away from the load.','Stop before posture breaks down, set the load down safely, and reset for the next walk.'],3),
('rjtuP6X','Walk Elliptical Cross Trainer','cardio','cardiovascular system',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','glutes','calves'],'elliptical machine',array['Set the resistance level and incline of the elliptical machine to your desired settings.','Get onto the pedals of the machine and grip the handles lightly.','Stand tall with the load secure and the shoulders level.','Walk at a controlled pace, keeping your shoulders level and your steps even.','Keep steps even and avoid leaning away from the load.','Stop before posture breaks down, set the load down safely, and reset for the next walk.'],0),
('rkg41Fb','Twin Handle Parallel Grip Lat Pulldown','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','rhomboids','rear deltoids'],'cable',array['Fit the seat to your body, then settle into the machine.','Hold the handles with palms facing down, hands about shoulder width.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Pull the handle down by driving your elbows toward your ribs; keep your torso steady.','Pull with the elbows rather than leaning far back to move the handle.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('RKjH6Lt','Side Bridge','waist','abdominals',array['obliques','glutes'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your side with your legs extended and stacked on top of each other.','Set your forearm on the ground directly below your shoulder, with your elbow bent at a 90-degree angle.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],0),
('rmEukuS','Single Leg Bridge with Outstretched Leg','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps'],'bodyweight',array['Settle onto your back with your knees bent and feet planted.','Reach one leg straight out in front of you.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('RoV1Rfa','Assisted Seated Pectoralis Major Stretch with Stability Ball','chest','pectorals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'assisted',array['Take a seat on a stability ball with your feet planted and your back straight.','Take a stability ball with both hands and extend your arms straight out in front of you.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('rQhGcin','Frog Planche','waist','abdominals',array['deltoids','pectorals','triceps'],'bodyweight',array['Set a straight-arm plank with the hands below the shoulders and the feet together.','Bend your elbows and lower your body toward the ground, with your spine steady.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],0),
('RQNVT10','Assisted Lying Gluteus and Piriformis Stretch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings'],'assisted',array['Settle onto your back with your legs extended.','Before moving, bend your right knee and place your right ankle on your left thigh, just above the knee.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Stay in a mild stretch rather than pulling farther with momentum.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('RqOtqD7','Cable Reverse Crunch','waist','abdominals',array['hip flexors'],'cable',array['Connect a cable to a low pulley and lie down facing up on a mat.','Take hold of the cable with both hands and extend your arms straight up toward the ceiling.','Set the pelvis and keep the neck relaxed before curling upward.','Curl your rib cage toward your pelvis, letting the abdominals move the torso.','Leave a little space between the chin and chest; keep the movement in the torso.','Lower the shoulders or torso with control before the next curl.'],0),
('rQxwMxO','Handstand Push-Up','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids','pectorals','core'],'bodyweight',array['Choose a wall and face away from it, standing a few feet away.','Set your hands on the ground about shoulder width and kick your feet up against the wall, coming into a handstand position.','Brace the abdomen and find a position you can maintain without holding your breath.','Brace your midsection and hold the position while breathing normally.','Keep breathing steadily as you maintain the same body line.','Keep the shape for the planned time, then come out of it with control.'],0),
('rR0LJzx','Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','erector spinae'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with palms facing down.','With your back straight and your core engaged, hinge at the hips and lower the dumbbells toward the ground, letting your knees to bend slightly.','Unlock the knees and brace the abdomen before moving the hips back.','Send your hips back with a soft knee bend, lowering the load close to your legs until the hamstrings stretch.','Keep the weight close to the legs and stop when the back would begin to round.','Drive the hips forward to stand tall without leaning back at the top.'],0),
('RrLske5','Bench Dip (Knees Bent)','upper arms','triceps',array['pectorals','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Take a seat on the edge of a bench or chair with your hands gripping the edge next to your hips.','Move your butt off the bench and straighten your legs in front of you, keeping your heels on the ground.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('RRWFUcw','Dumbbell Lunge','upper legs','glutes',array['quadriceps','hamstrings','calves'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand.','Step forward with your right foot, lowering your body into a lunge position.','Set your stance wide enough to balance before bending either knee.','Step into the movement and bend both knees, keeping your front foot planted.','Keep the front foot planted and avoid collapsing inward at the knee.','Push through the lead foot to return to the start, then change legs as planned.'],26),
('rseLfH3','Kettlebell Extended Range Single-Arm Press on Floor','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'kettlebell',array['Begin by lying on your back on the floor with your knees bent and feet planted.','Take a kettlebell in one hand, with your palm facing toward your feet.','Brace the torso and align the wrists with the forearms.','Press the weight or handles away while keeping your trunk braced.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower the weight to its starting height under control before pressing again; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('RSOsp5d','Dumbbell Standing Around World','shoulders','deltoids',array['triceps','forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and hold a dumbbell in each hand.','Reach your arms straight out to the sides at shoulder height, palms facing down.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Guide the weights through a broad circular arc without leaning or swinging.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
('rTbyBYV','Exercise Ball Lying Side Lat Stretch','back','latissimus dorsi',array['deltoids','triceps'],'stability ball',array['Settle onto your side with your legs extended and your head supported by the stability ball.','Set your top arm on the ball for stability.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('RtyAsy1','Arms Apart Circular Toe Touch','upper legs','glutes',array['hamstrings','quadriceps','calves'],'bodyweight',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width and arms extended to the sides.','With your legs straight, bend forward at the waist and reach down toward your toes with your right hand.','Soften the knees and let the hips start the fold.','Fold forward from the hips and let your hands travel toward your feet without forcing the reach.','Keep the movement controlled throughout the range.','Hold briefly at a comfortable depth, then rise by extending the hips.'],0),
('rUXfn3R','Machine Back Extension','back','erector spinae',array['glutes','hamstrings'],'leverage machine',array['Set the machine to fit your body size and range of motion.','Take a seat on the machine with your back against the pad and your feet secured.','Secure the hips and feet on the support before lifting.','Raise your torso or legs until they line up with your body, without arching sharply at the lower back.','Finish in a straight body line, before the lower back overarches.','Ease back to the start before repeating.'],0),
('RVwzP10','Cable Pulldown','back','latissimus dorsi',array['biceps','forearms'],'cable',array['Set the cable pulldown machine so that the seat is at a comfortable height and the knee pad is secured.','Take a seat on the seat with your back straight and your feet planted.','Sit tall and set the shoulders before drawing the handle down.','Pull the handle down by driving your elbows toward your ribs; keep your torso steady.','Pull with the elbows rather than leaning far back to move the handle.','Let the handle rise steadily until the arms are long, then reset the shoulders.'],0),
('rWoBmi5','Korean Dips','chest','pectorals',array['triceps','deltoids'],'bodyweight',array['Set yourself between two parallel bars with your arms extended and supporting your body weight.','Before moving, lower your body by bending your elbows until your upper arms are parallel to the ground.','Set the shoulders down and keep the elbows pointed mostly behind you.','Bend the elbows to lower between the supports; stop at a comfortable shoulder depth.','Choose a depth that lets the shoulders stay comfortable.','Press through the hands to rise, then reset the shoulders before another rep.'],0),
('RYcV1kH','Barbell Squat Jump Step Rear Lunge','upper legs','quadriceps',array['glutes','hamstrings','calves'],'barbell',array['Begin by standing with your feet about shoulder width, holding a barbell across your upper back.','Before moving, lower your body into a squat position by bending your knees and pushing your hips back.','Brace the abdomen and spread pressure across the whole foot.','Bend at the hips and knees to lower, keeping your feet grounded and knees tracking with the toes.','Drive upward with the chest and hips rising together; keep the knees from collapsing inward.','Stand fully, reset your footing and breathing, then begin the next descent.'],0),
('rZ80Gbp','Cable Seated Single-Arm Concentration Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'cable',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; your back straight.','Take a cable handle with one hand and place your elbow on the inside of your thigh, just above the knee.','Set the shoulders and upper arms before bending the elbows.','Bend your elbows to bring the weight toward your shoulders without swinging your torso.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('s0HKO2I','Bodyweight Kneeling Triceps Extension','upper arms','triceps',array['deltoids','pectorals'],'bodyweight',array['Get down on the ground with your knees about hip width.','Set your hands on the ground in front of you, about shoulder width, fingers pointing forward.','Set the upper arms in place before extending the elbows.','Keep the upper arms steady and extend through the elbows to move the weight.','Keep the upper arms steady while the forearms travel.','Bend the elbows slowly to return to the start of the next rep.'],0),
