('SxHteRW','Dumbbell Standing Alternate Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Stand and set your feet about shoulder width, holding a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing your body.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and your core engaged.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the weights away from your torso to about shoulder height, keeping the elbows softly bent.','Finish one side''s motion before the other side takes over.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
('sxY5Biu','Dumbbell Single-Arm Zottman Preacher Curl','upper arms','biceps',array['forearms'],'dumbbell',array['Take a seat on a preacher curl bench and hold a dumbbell in one hand with palms facing up.','Set your upper arm on the preacher bench pad, letting your arm to fully extend.','Set the working upper arm against the preacher pad and leave the elbow free to bend.','Curl palms-up, turn the palms down at the top, and lower with that overhand grip.','Keep both shoulders level and resist turning toward the working arm.','Lower until the elbows are nearly straight, keeping the upper arms still; switch sides when the set calls for it.'],0),
