('yRpV5TC','Shoulder Tap','waist','abdominals',array['deltoids','triceps'],'bodyweight',array['Begin in a high plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body in a straight line.','Brace your trunk and lift your right hand off the ground, reaching across to tap your left shoulder.','Brace the trunk lightly before moving a limb.','Move the working arm or leg while keeping the trunk steady and the breathing even.','Keep the pelvis from rocking as the arm or leg moves.','Reset your posture before changing sides or beginning the next rep.'],0),
('yRYyfdA','Exercise Ball Seated Hamstring Stretch','upper legs','hamstrings',array['glutes','erector spinae'],'stability ball',array['Take a seat on the stability ball with your feet planted and your knees bent at a 90-degree angle.','With control roll the ball forward, walking your feet out until your upper back is resting on the ball and your legs are extended straight in front of you.','Settle into the starting position and take an easy breath before moving deeper.','Ease toward the stretch until you feel mild tension; keep breathing and avoid bouncing.','Keep the ball steady and use the feet to manage your balance.','Hold the position with steady breathing, then release gently; repeat on the other side if needed.'],0),
('Ys97II0','Dumbbell Seated Front Raise','shoulders','deltoids',array['trapezius','biceps'],'dumbbell',array['Plant both feet while seated on a bench; a dumbbell in each hand, resting on your thighs.','Keep your spine in a comfortable neutral position and core engaged.','Start with a manageable load and a small bend in the elbows.','Lift the arms forward to about shoulder height, keeping the ribs down and torso still.','Stop near shoulder height rather than shrugging to lift higher.','Lower the arms slowly to your sides without swinging the weight.'],0),
